{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:version-negotiation.1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:connections.2", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:framing.3"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "the handshake the artifact's first states describe: a protocol header each way, then an open carrying the container-id the declared surface makes mandatory", "start": "connection:START", "steps": [{"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001402000000005310c00701a10474657374", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPEN_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}], "vector": "slice-open-close-handshake"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:connections.2"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "open with no container-id is refused \u2014 the one field the declared surface makes mandatory on that performative, and the one a peer cannot infer \u2014 while the same peer admits the same open once the field is there, which is what makes the refusal a rule rather than a blanket dislike of opens", "start": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "steps": [{"bytes": "0000000e02000000005310c00100", "direction": "send", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "refused"}}, {"bytes": "0000001402000000005310c00701a10474657374", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPEN_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}], "vector": "slice-open-missing-container-id"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:connections.1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "channel-max declares a `ushort` and the frame carries a `ulong` of 70000, which no ushort can hold: a value of the wrong declared type is a field-value violation, and the contrast step shows the same open admitted once the field carries its own type", "start": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "steps": [{"bytes": "0000001f02000000005310c01204a104746573744040800000000000011170", "direction": "send", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "refused"}}, {"bytes": "0000001902000000005310c00c04a104746573744040600001", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPEN_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}], "vector": "slice-open-channel-max-wrong-type"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.3"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "a peer that received sasl-mechanisms is the SASL client, and a challenge is the server's performative: the frame is well formed and the direction is wrong. The condition is amqp:illegal-state and not framing-error: the frame is well formed and its direction is wrong, which is the artifact's 'not permitted in the current state', while framing-error's definition is about forming a frame header from the stream. The layer's other state refusals name the same condition, so the SASL dialogue's moment rules stay one rule rather than two", "start": "connection:START", "steps": [{"bytes": "414d515003010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515003010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001c02010000005340c00f01c00c01a309414e4f4e594d4f5553", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001302010000005342c00601c00301a000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:illegal-state", "reason": "illegalState", "status": "refused"}}], "vector": "slice-sasl-challenge-from-client"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.3"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "the artifact says the mechanisms list cannot be null or empty: a field-value constraint, so invalid-field rather than the wire-level condition. The exchange negotiates the SASL layer first, because a SASL performative in the AMQP layer is refused as illegalState \u2014 a rule this vector met before it met the one it tests. The refusal ends the connection rather than discarding, because no open has been exchanged: the error-triggered close has nothing to discard, which is why this vector cannot also carry an admitted contrast \u2014 that role belongs to the challenge exchange, which receives a well-formed list first", "start": "connection:START", "steps": [{"bytes": "414d515003010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515003010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000000f02010000005340c0020145", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "connection:END", "status": "refused"}}], "vector": "slice-sasl-mechanisms-empty"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:version-negotiation.1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "an open before the protocol header: the frame is well formed and the moment is wrong, which the artifact defines as amqp:illegal-state \u2014 'the peer sent a frame that is not permitted in the current state' \u2014 and not as amqp:connection:framing-error, which is 'a valid frame header cannot be formed'. The contrast step sends the header from the same state and is admitted, so the refusal is about the order and not the frame", "start": "connection:START", "steps": [{"bytes": "0000001502000000005310c00801a10570726f6265", "direction": "send", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:illegal-state", "reason": "illegalState", "state": "connection:START", "status": "refused"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}], "vector": "slice-open-before-header"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.10", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:open/field:channel-max.2"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "the peer's open declares channel-max 1, and the frame that follows is on channel 2, one above the highest channel the peer permitted \u2014 the only channel value where a bound widened by one differs, since anything further above it is refused by the true bound too", "start": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPEN_SENT", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 16}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "probe", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 4096}, {"type": "ushort", "value": 1}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 0, "doff": 2, "payload": "", "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000000005310c01004a10470656572407000001000600001", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPENED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "limit", "status": "refused"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 17}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "uint", "value": 16}, {"type": "uint", "value": 16}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 2, "doff": 2, "payload": "", "type": "00"}}], "vector": "exchange-session-channel-above-the-declared-bound"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.30"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "the peer's flow sets the remote window to one transfer and grants credit of ten, so the second transfer we send is refused by the window and not by the link's credit \u2014 the difference a credit mutation would otherwise hide", "start": "session:UNMAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:BEGIN_SENT", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 17}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"type": "null"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "uint", "value": 16}, {"type": "uint", "value": 16}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "payload": "", "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000002002000001005311c01304600001700000000070000000107000000010", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "probe", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": false}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "payload": "", "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001b02000001005312c00e03a10570726f6265700000000041", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000003102000001005313c02407700000000070000000017000000000700000001070000000007000000000700000000a", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 20}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "uint", "v